Subject: [PATCH] fix(skills): correct orphans mapping + gate status doc +
 worktree/gates routing

Second review round on #430 (Codex + CodeRabbit), all verified against source:
- coverage.json: revert orphans -> issue-basics. 'orphans' is 'forge issue orphans'
  (dangling dependency edges, lib/commands/_issue.js), an issue command, not
  worktree reaping. Earlier round mis-mapped it to worktree.
- using-forge.js: issue-basics gains orphan/dangling cues so 'show orphan issues'
  routes (discoverability); worktree gains diagnostic + 'forge worktree' anchors
  (restores the 'worktree miss its node_modules' should_trigger fixture that the
  bare-'worktree' removal broke); gates gains 'forge gate'/'gate check'/'gate
  status' command anchors.
- gates/SKILL.md: 'forge gate status' also requires <issue-id> (handleStatus
  rejects a missing id), same as 'gate check'.
- regenerate worktree(83)/gates(84) scorecards; .agents synced by hook.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
